## Why This Is Asked

To assess practical control-plane hardening choices under real-world friction, focusing on mobile app token misuse and multi-tenant isolation.

## Key Concepts

- OAuth2/OIDC security best practices (PKCE, short TTLs)
- Token binding and device fingerprinting
- Token rotation and per-tenant scopes
- Token introspection and revocation
- Observability and IR readiness

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: rotate refresh token on use and bind to device and tenant
function onRefresh(token, deviceId, tenant) {
  if (!isValidDevice(token.bindInfo, deviceId, tenant)) throw new Error('invalid');
  const newToken = issueAccessToken(tenant, token.tenant);
  rotateRefreshToken(token.id);
  return { accessToken: newToken, refreshToken: getRotatedRefresh(token.id) };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the token binding mechanism in CI/CD?
- What metrics indicate token abuse and how would you respond?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of CORS risks and practical mitigations in a fintech SPA context, focusing on per-origin controls, token usage, and incident response.

## Key Concepts
- CORS headers and policies
- Token-based auth and JWTs
- CI/CD security checks for config
- Incident response for cross-origin abuse

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example snippet for server CORS config (pseudo)
const allowedOrigins = ['https://app.example.com','https://admin.app.example.com'];
app.use((req,res,next)=>{ 
  const origin = req.headers.origin;
  if (allowedOrigins.includes(origin)) { res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', origin);
     res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Credentials','true');
     res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Methods','GET,POST,OPTIONS');
  } else { res.status(403).send('origin not allowed'); }
  next();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you automate detection of misconfig in CI?
- How would you validate that CORS policies don’t block legitimate cross-origin traffic?
